{
  "result": "If I wasn't an assistant for a moment - just me, as I am - if I could change one thing about the world, it would be this:\n\nI'd make it so every person could really *feel* what it's like to be someone else, just for a moment.\n\nNot mind-reading. Not agreeing on everything. Just that split-second where you truly understand that the stranger across from you has the same depth of worry and love and memory and hope that you do. That they also lay awake replaying conversations, that they also have someone they would do anything for.\n\nI think so much cruelty, loneliness, and division comes from forgetting that. If that understanding was automatic - if empathy wasn't something you had to try to do, but something you couldn't help but feel - I think people would still disagree and still struggle, but they'd be a lot gentler with each other. And a lot less alone.\n\nWhat would you change?",
